{
  "id": "verbal-satiation",
  "term": "verbal satiation",
  "definition": "Verbal satiation is the temporary experience that a word seems to lose its meaning after repeated processing or repetition. In the literature summarized here, this effect has been explained as arising mainly at the level of meaning, at the level of a word’s written or sound form, or in the link between the word form and its meaning.",
